<title>CANADA: Imperial Life Assurance Co 1996 profit rises.</title>
<headline>Imperial Life Assurance Co 1996 profit rises.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1997-02-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Imperial Life Assurance Co of Canada said net income rose to C$13.7 million in the year ended December 31, up from C$1.0 million in 1995.</p>
<p>Imperial Life said in a statement its improved results were due to higher investment income resulting from the sale of its foreign operations, lower loan losses and reduced administrative and tax costs.</p>
<p>The insurer's bottom line was also helped by distribution costs incurred last year and the acquisition of a block of business.</p>
<p>((Reuters Toronto Bureau (416) 941-8100))</p>
</text>
